Description: Disable clang-format during distribution to prevent OOM
 When make_distrib.py runs, it calls clang_format_inplace() for each C/C++
 header file in the distribution. This resolves to depot-tools/clang_format.py
 which is a Python wrapper that runs gclient_paths.py to find clang-format.
 .
 On systems without the bundled clang-format binary (like Debian builds using
 tarballs instead of gclient sync), each clang_format.py process runs
 'git rev-parse' and other subprocesses to search for clang-format. With
 16,000+ header files, this spawns 16,000+ Python processes simultaneously,
 consuming ~320GB virtual memory and triggering the OOM killer.
 .
 The --no-format flag skips clang-format entirely. This is safe because:
 - Headers are already properly formatted by upstream CEF
 - Distribution headers are read-only for end users
 - clang-format is purely cosmetic and doesn't affect functionality
Author: Juan Manuel Mendez Rey <juan.mendezr@proton.me>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-01-04

diff --git a/cef/tools/automate/automate-git.py b/cef/tools/automate/automate-git.py
index 9ce3557..84cf0b9 100644
--- a/cef/tools/automate/automate-git.py
+++ b/cef/tools/automate/automate-git.py
@@ -1940,6 +1940,11 @@ if not options.nodistrib and (chromium_checkout_changed or \
     if options.nodebugbuild or options.noreleasebuild or type != 'standard':
       path += ' --allow-partial'
     path += ' --ninja-build'
+    # Disable clang-format during distribution to prevent spawning thousands of
+    # clang_format.py processes. Each process runs git commands via gclient_paths,
+    # causing memory exhaustion on systems without bundled clang-format binary.
+    # Headers are already properly formatted by upstream CEF.
+    path += ' --no-format'
     if options.x64build:
       path += ' --x64-build'
     elif options.armbuild:
